# Naval Estimates: The Dreadnought Age — desktop releases

Download page for the desktop build of *Naval Estimates*, a turn-based
grand-strategy naval game set in 1900–1950: design guns, turrets and ships on
physics-based models and run a navy through the dreadnought age. This
repository holds only the release archives; the game is developed elsewhere.

**Browser version:** [itch.io](https://elouda.itch.io/naval-estimates) ·
**Website:** [navalestimates.com](https://navalestimates.com/) ·
**Community:** [Discord](https://discord.gg/rKDwhXuwUR)

## Download

Every version is under [Releases](https://github.com/Elouda/nereleases/releases),
with one archive per platform:

| Platform | File |
|---|---|
| Windows (x64) | `NavalEstimates-<version>-win-x64.zip` |
| macOS (Intel and Apple Silicon) | `NavalEstimates-<version>-mac-universal.zip` |
| Linux (x64) | `NavalEstimates-<version>-linux-x64.tar.gz` |

Extract the archive anywhere and run the app inside it. There is no installer
and nothing else to install.

The archives are not code-signed yet, so Windows and macOS warn on the first
launch. On Windows choose "More info", then "Run anyway". On macOS, if the app
is blocked, open System Settings → Privacy & Security and choose "Open Anyway".

## Updating

Close the game and extract the new archive over the old folder. Your saves are
not in that folder: they live in the app's data directory
(`%APPDATA%\Naval Estimates` on Windows,
`~/Library/Application Support/Naval Estimates` on macOS,
`~/.config/Naval Estimates` on Linux) and survive updates and reinstalls.

Moving over from the browser version? Export the campaign from its save slot
on itch.io and import it in the desktop app. The reverse works the same way.

## Patch notes

Patch notes are published on the itch.io devlog and the website, not here. A
release on this page carries the archives alone.
